### Book Reviews REST API - request collection
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, and imports into Postman (Admin > Import).
### Run the requests top to bottom: the login response gives you the token, paste it into @token.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@username = alice
@password = wonderland
@isbn = 9780141439518

### 1. Register a new user  ->  201 {message, user:{username}}
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2. Register a duplicate username  ->  409 {message}
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 3. Login  ->  200 {accessToken, tokenType, expiresIn}   (copy accessToken into @token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 4. Login with a wrong password  ->  401 {message}
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 5. Get the list of all books, each one carries its real ISBN-13  ->  200 [book, book, ...]
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 6. Get a book by ISBN-13  ->  200 book
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/{{isbn}}

### 7. The same book by hyphenated ISBN, with spaces, and by ISBN-10  ->  200 book
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/978-0-14-143951-8
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/978 0 14 143951 8
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/0141439513

### 8. The same book by the legacy numeric id, 1 to 10  ->  200 book
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/8

### 9. A well formed ISBN that no book uses  ->  404 {message}
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/9780000000000

### 10. Something that is not an ISBN at all  ->  400 {message}
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/abc

### 11. Get books by author, case insensitive, partial name allowed  ->  200 [book, ...]
GET {{baseUrl}}/author/Unknown

### 12. Get books by title, case insensitive, partial title allowed  ->  200 [book, ...]
GET {{baseUrl}}/title/the

### 13. A name that is only whitespace  ->  400 {message}. It is rejected before the
###     data source is read, so a blank search cannot quietly match every author
###     that has a space in the name. Left alone it answered 200 with 6 books.
GET {{baseUrl}}/author/%20

### 14. The same for a title. Left alone, a blank title matched all 10 books.
GET {{baseUrl}}/title/%20

### 15. A padded but real name is trimmed and still matches  ->  200 [book, ...]
GET {{baseUrl}}/author/%20Jane%20Austen%20

### 16. Get all reviews of a book  ->  200 { "alice": {username, rating, review} }
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/{{isbn}}

### 17. Get one user's review of a book  ->  200 { "alice": {username, rating, review} }
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/{{isbn}}?username={{username}}

### 18. Get the initial, never edited, reviews of every book, keyed by ISBN
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/initial

### 19. Add a review, requires a token  ->  201 {username, rating, review, message}
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/{{isbn}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5,
  "review": "A masterpiece, read it twice."
}

### 20. Add a second review for the same book  ->  409 {message}, use the PUT request instead
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/{{isbn}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 3,
  "review": "A duplicate of my own review."
}

### 21. Add a review with an out of range rating  ->  400 {message}
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/{{isbn}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 42,
  "review": "Rating must be 1 to 5."
}

### 22. Add a review for a malformed ISBN  ->  400 {message}
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/not-an-isbn
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "review": "The ISBN is malformed."
}

### 23. Add a review without a token  ->  401 {message}
POST {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/{{isbn}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "review": "No token supplied."
}

### 24. Modify your own review, here sent as a hyphenated ISBN  ->  200 {username, rating, review, modified:true, message}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/978-0-14-143951-8
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "review": "Still a masterpiece on a reread."
}

### 25. Step 24 removed this review from /review/initial, step 18 proves it
GET {{baseUrl}}/review/initial

### 26. Modify a book you have not reviewed  ->  404 {message}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/9780140447699
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 4,
  "review": "Nothing to modify here."
}

### 27. Delete your own review, here sent as the ISBN-10  ->  200 {message}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/0141439513
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 28. Delete it again  ->  404 {message}
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/customer/auth/review/{{isbn}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### The HTML pages under /ui. Open these in a browser rather than
### sending them from here, so the session cookie is kept and the
### flash message banner is visible. The REST Client cannot show the
### banner, it only shows the page source.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 29. The book list page
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/books

### 30. A book page, no reviews yet and no session, so it invites you to log in
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}

### 31. The log in and register page
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/login

### 32. Logged in, the book page offers the add review form
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}

### 33. Post the add form. It redirects to the book page, which shows
###     the message banner "Review by <user> added to the book with
###     ISBN ..." above the reviews, with the new review among them.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}/review
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

rating=5&review=A masterpiece from a form.

### 34. Post it again  ->  redirected back with "You have already reviewed
###     the book with ISBN ... Use PUT to modify it." in the banner
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}/review
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

rating=3&review=A duplicate of my own review.

### 35. Post the edit form. The banner reads "Review by <user> updated on
###     the book with ISBN ..." and the review below shows the new text
###     and an "edited" tag.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}/review/edit
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

rating=4&review=Still a masterpiece on a reread.

### 36. Post the delete form. The banner reads "Review by <user> removed
###     from the book with ISBN ..." and the review is gone from the list.
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}/review/delete

### 37. Post it again  ->  redirected back with "You have not reviewed
###     the book with ISBN ... yet." in the banner
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}/review/delete

### 38. A rating outside 1 to 5  ->  "'rating' must be an integer between 1 and 5."
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/{{isbn}}/review
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

rating=42&review=Out of range.

### 39. The pages redirect to the book list with a banner when the ISBN is unknown
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/books/9999999999999

### 40. A page that does not exist, same treatment
GET {{baseUrl}}/ui/nowhere

### 41. Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/ui/logout

### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### The read-only data route under /internal. The public book routes
### read the catalogue from here with Axios rather than from the
### in-memory store. These are here to show what they are reading.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------

### 42. Everything the public routes read for GET /, GET /author/:author and GET /title/:title
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/books

### 43. What GET /isbn/:isbn reads, and the answers it relays
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/books/isbn/{{isbn}}
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/books/isbn/abc
###
GET {{baseUrl}}/internal/books/isbn/9780000000000

### 44. A read whose data source is unreachable. Start the server with
###     BOOKS_DATA_URL pointing somewhere dead, for example
###     BOOKS_DATA_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1/internal npm start
###     and any of steps 5 to 15 answers 502 {message} instead.
GET {{baseUrl}}/isbn/{{isbn}}
